---
import { PLAN_LIMITS, PRODUCT_MODELS, PRODUCT_MODEL_INFO } from '@golem/shared';
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE } from '../../lib/studio-plugin';

// "when to use Plan, Agent or Super Agent" — the third is in PRODUCT_MODES, which is every mode
// the system can produce, and not in PRODUCT_MODES_OFFERED, which is what a person may pick. The
// free allowance beside it was equally stale: it read 60 Credits against a free tier repriced to
// PLAN_LIMITS.free.creditsPerDay. Both are read now, so neither can be left behind again.
const modeNames = new Intl.ListFormat('en', { type: 'disjunction' }).format(
  PRODUCT_MODELS.map((m) => PRODUCT_MODEL_INFO[m].name),
);
/*
 * THE BODY WAS GATED AND THE METADATA WAS NOT, WHICH IS THE HALF PEOPLE ACTUALLY SHARE.
 *
 * A <meta name="description"> and its og:description twin are what a search result and a pasted
 * link show. This page's body has asked STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE since the listing was removed,
 * while its description went on promising a Creator Store install path in every snippet — so the
 * promise reached the reader BEFORE the correction did, and the correction only arrived if they
 * clicked. Same constant, same answer, one sentence earlier.
 */
const free = PLAN_LIMITS.free;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting started — Apple Docs"
  description={STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE
    ? 'From signup to your first AI-built feature in Roblox Studio: create an account, make a project, install the plugin, pair, and chat your first build.'
    : 'From signup to your first conversation with Apple: create an account, make a project and start chatting. Public Studio installation is unavailable, so the Studio steps apply only to an existing working plugin.'}
  heading="Getting started"
>
  <p>
    Create your workspace, start a conversation, and check Studio availability before building.
  </p>

  {!STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE && <div class="callout"><p><strong>Public Studio installation is unavailable.</strong> Steps 1–2 work now. Continue to the Studio steps only if you already have a working plugin. New users can chat, but must wait for an approved public plugin before Apple can change their place. <a href="/docs/plugin">See installation status</a>.</p></div>}

  <h2>1. Create an account</h2>
  <p>
    Go to <a href="/app">the app</a> and sign up with an email address and a password. That is the
    whole form — no card, no phone number. You start with your full daily allowance of
    <strong>{free.creditsPerDay} Credits</strong> immediately.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Create a project</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>project</strong> is Apple's workspace for one Roblox place: its chat history, its
    checkpoints, and its memory of what you have built together. Click
    <strong>New project</strong>, give it a name (naming it after the place helps), and you land in
    the chat workspace.
  </p>
  <p>
    Projects are unlimited on the free tier, so make one per place rather than reusing a single
    project — the per-project memory works much better that way.
  </p>

  <h2>3. {STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE ? 'Install the Studio plugin' : 'Check Studio availability'}</h2>
  <p>
    {STUDIO_PLUGIN_STORE_LIVE ? <>Apple changes your place through the <strong>Apple for Studio</strong> plugin. Follow <a href="/docs/plugin">the Creator Store installation steps</a> before continuing.</> : <>There is no working public Creator Store installation path right now. If you do not already have the plugin, stop here and use the chat workspace. Check <a href="/docs/plugin">plugin status</a> for availability; the remaining steps describe connecting an existing working installation.</>}
  </p>

  <h2>4. Connect it to your project</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open your place in Roblox Studio and click <strong>Apple</strong> in the Plugins tab.</li>
    <li>
      In the Apple web workspace, open the project and press <strong>Enter pairing code</strong> in
      the <strong>Connect Roblox Studio</strong> block. You get a six-character code like
      <code>K7M3QP</code>.
    </li>
    <li>Type the code into the Apple panel in Studio and press <strong>Connect</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The workspace shows your place name and the panel turns green. Codes expire after 10 minutes; if
    yours does, generate another. More detail on <a href="/docs/connect">Connect a project</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Ask for your first build</h2>
  <p>Choose <strong>Apple</strong> for limited free use, or <strong>Apple MAX</strong> with an eligible paid subscription, and describe what you want:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>“make a lobby with a spinning obby door”</li>
    <li>“add a coin leaderboard that saves between sessions”</li>
    <li>“the kill brick in Workspace.Stage2 doesn't kill — fix it”</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Watch the compact activity line and open details when needed. A chat response alone is not
    proof that your place changed: check the reported result, then test it in Studio.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Iterate like you mean it</h2>
  <p>
    The first result is a first draft. React to it the way you would with a collaborator: “make
    the door slower”, “the door should only open for players with the key”. Apple keeps the
    context of everything it has done in this project.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Safety net:</strong> every individual change is one native undo step
      (<kbd>Ctrl+Z</kbd> / <kbd>⌘Z</kbd> in Studio), so undoing a whole run means one press per
      step. Apple also checkpoints your place before every agent run, and restoring that checkpoint
      from the workspace sidebar takes the whole run back at once — even days later.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Where next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/modes">Models</a> — when to use {modeNames}.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/credits-and-limits">Credits &amp; limits</a> — how far {free.creditsPerDay} Credits goes.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/updating">Updating the plugin</a> — Roblox will not do it for you.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a> — when the panel says something you didn't expect.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
